vtun (3.0.4+fork3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Never tunnel link-local multicast read from the local tun (IPv4
    224.0.0.0/24, IPv6 ff02::/16). Modern kernels emit an autoconf burst
    (IPv6 Router Solicitation + MLDv2, IPv4 IGMPv3) the instant a freshly
    created tun comes up; forwarding it into the tunnel hits the peer's
    still-DOWN tun ("Input/output error (5)") and made slower clients
    reconnect-loop against hubs running a current OS. Wire protocol
    unchanged; global-scope multicast and unicast are unaffected.
  * Log each message once: drop LOG_PERROR from openlog(), which doubled
    every journal line under systemd foreground (-n) operation (syslog
    socket + stderr both captured).
  * Packaging: ship a tmpfiles.d snippet creating /run/lock/vtund —
    /var/lock is a tmpfs on modern systems and the directory was missing,
    so server-side auth failed with "Can't create temp lock file".
    Also create the stats directory /var/log/vtund.

 -- Dirk Tostmann <tostmann@gmail.com>  Sat, 06 Jun 2026 09:15:00 +0000

vtun (3.0.4+fork2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native systemd units: vtund.service (standalone server) and
    vtund-client@.service (per-session client template), installed disabled.
  * Ship /etc/vtund.conf as a conffile (default config the units read).
  * CI derives the package version from the git tag (vX.Y.Z -> X.Y.Z).

 -- Dirk Tostmann <tostmann@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 21:30:00 +0000

vtun (3.0.4+fork1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Maintained fork making vtun build and run on modern systems (OpenSSL 3.x,
    GCC 14+, Debian 13 "trixie", Ubuntu 24.04). Fixes the OpenSSL 3 Blowfish
    crash by loading the legacy provider in-process before daemonising and
    porting the EVP cipher code to the opaque OpenSSL 1.1+/3.x API; fixes the
    non-ECB modes (CBC/CFB/OFB) via a correct htonl() prototype
    (<arpa/inet.h>); builds cleanly on GCC 14 (-fcommon, prototype includes,
    C99 inline fix); repairs HAVE_WORKING_FORK detection for standalone-server
    (-s) mode and up/down scripts; and refreshes config.guess/config.sub for
    aarch64/arm64.

 -- Dirk Tostmann <tostmann@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
